 ('charge-unit','Figure 5 caption and body print mC/cm² for 1.6/3.6/8.3/18.7 and 222 per monolayer; Figures 7/9 explicitly print µC/cm². Do not silently normalize source charge units.',[6,7,8]),
 ('coverage-not-area','Equivalent monolayers are upper-bound charge-derived amounts assuming 100% efficiency, not measured planar-area fraction or exact shell thickness.',[7]),
 ('figure7-count','Four histograms and four listed pulse durations appear, although Figure 7 caption says five samples. Five random image fields per sample is a different count.',[8]),
 ('figure7-values','First histogram mean/sigma are 2.2/2.4 nm; body gives smallest height 2.4 and spread 2 nm. Largest histogram sigma 6.1 nm versus rounded body 6 nm.',[7,8]),
 ('figure8-caption','Figure 8 actual ordinate is particle density, not captioned mean height. The height-distribution ±sigma wording cannot establish the density error-bar statistic.',[8]),
 ('rate-time-unit','Body nucleation-rate range uses cm−2 ms−1; summary uses cm−2 s−1 with rounded values. Both are retained as conflicting source statements.',[8,9]),
 ('density-summaries','Abstract, body and summary give different rounded initial/saturation ranges. Current-model N∞ is approximately an order of magnitude above microscopy density.',[1,5,8,9]),
 ('induction-vs-2ms-image','Body says no Ag before 2–3 ms while Figure 5 includes a 2 ms image; low-end object density is close to contamination background. No detection-corrected nucleus count is provided.',[5,6,8,9]),
 ('height-width-geometry','NC-AFM height is measured; tip-convolved width is not true diameter. Approximately spherical diameter-as-height rationale differs from the hemispherical height-as-radius model.',[7,8,9]),
 ('tem-afm-scope','TEM 10–25 Å objects have unspecified pulse duration and were mechanically transferred. They are not a verified same-sample match to 2–20 nm AFM height populations.',[5,7]),
 ('diffraction-reference','Table 1 expected spacings and intensities are ICDD reference values, not measured specimen intensities. Printed 111 reference spacing is 2.32 Å and must not be silently repaired.',[7]),
 ('oxide-name','Aqueous instability paragraph names AgO; later phase test contrasts Ag0 with Ag2O. The metallic SAED assignment is retained without creating an oxide synthesis record.',[3,5]),
 ('equation2-inputs','Printed Equation 2 contains A and lacks the explicit F factor present in Equation 1. A is not defined numerically; exact reproduction of N∞ is not supported by note 43 alone.',[4,5]),
